    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIAtr">III Atr</ref> 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="230" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hwa þeof clænsian wylle, lecge an C to wedde, healf landrican ⁊ healf cinges gerefan binnan port, ⁊ gange to þrimfealdan ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="230" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis furem innoxiare uelit, ponat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IIIAtr_7.lnote.oe.10"/> unum hundretum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IIIAtr_7.lnote.oe.11"/> in uadio, dimidium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IIIAtr_7.lnote.oe.12"/> tunc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IIIAtr_7.lnote.oe.13"/> domino, dimidium preposito regis intra portum, et adeat triplex ordalium.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="7" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="68" ed="#robertson"/>And gif hwa þeof clænsian wylle, lecge an C to wedde, healf landrican ⁊ healf cinges gerefan binnan port, ⁊ gange to þrimfealdan ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="231" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn jemand einen [hingerichteten] Dieb als rein erweisen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.1"/> will, so hinterlege er Ein Hundert [Silbers<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.2"/>] als Pfand<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.3"/>, halb<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.4"/> dem Immunitätsherrn und halb dem Königsvogt innerhalb der [fürs Ordal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.5"/> zuständigen Gerichts]stadt, und schreite zu dreifachem Ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone wishes to prove an [executed] thief innocent, let him deposit one hundred [of silver] as a pledge, half to the lord of the immunity and half to the king's reeve within the [court-]town [responsible for the ordeal], and go to the threefold ordeal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIIAtr_7.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="69" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone seeks to clear a thief, he shall deposit 100 [of silver] as security<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIIAtr_7.robnote.n.2"/>, half with the lord of the manor<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IIIAtr_7.robnote.n.3"/> and half with the king's town-reeve<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IIIAtr_7.robnote.n.4"/> and he shall go to the triple ordeal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="446" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone wishes to clear a thief, he is to lay down a hundred [of silver] as a pledge, half for the lord of the estate and half for the king’s reeve in the town, and to go to the three-fold ordeal.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="372"><ref target="clause:Wal_part-001">Wal</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">230</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">un. h. in uadium ponat <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">un. h. in uadium ponat <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">230</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dretum <hi rend="italic">M</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dretum <hi rend="italic">M</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">230</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">230</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">tun <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">tun <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">160</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hier leistet Kläger Ordal (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 18b), aber nur als Vertreter des toten Verklagten. Bei Ine und Æthelstan aber auch in Normannenzeit reinigt der Eid den Hingerichteten; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4; Tote 1ff.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Here the plaintiff undergoes the ordeal (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 18b), but only as representative of the dead accused. In Ine and Æthelstan, however, and also in the Norman period, the oath clears the executed man; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4; Tote 1ff.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">160</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 1, 1⁴</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 1, 1⁴</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">160</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Prozessualpfand (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5) beträgt soviel wie er, wenn Klage missglückt, verlieren wird nach 7, 1. Dieser Verlust ist in ECf 36, 2 sein Wergeld. Vermutlich ist auch hier 8 ℔ Wergeld (<hi rend="italic">s. d</hi>. 8b) der Denalagu</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The procedural pledge (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5) amounts to as much as he will lose, according to 7, 1, if the claim fails. In ECf 36, 2 this loss is his wergild. Presumably here too it is the wergild of 8 ℔ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 8b) of the Danelaw</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">160</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. 3, 2⁶·⁷</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 3, 2⁶·⁷</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">160</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 6, 1³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 6, 1³</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. In. 20–21, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">This sum is forfeited if the plea miscarries, cf. 7, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. 3, 2.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIAtr_7.robnote.n.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. 6, 1 and note.</seg></note>
      </div>
